  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"The host needs a current list of guests, including whether they are ready to join a game or prefer to settle in first.\", \"decision\": \"How should guests make their arrival known?\", \"goal\": \"Help guests find compatible games, understand how to play, and enjoy the evening without avoidable waiting or confusion.\", \"problem\": \"A community room is hosting an evening of board games for adults with different levels of experience. Several tables, a host, willing game teachers, short waiting activities, and a varied collection are available. Guests can decline any game and join a later one. Every game has an agreed latest stopping time before the room closes, and ordinary refreshments and conversation have their own small areas.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nThe host greets each arriving guest and records their name and readiness on the welcome sheet. A brief personal exchange gives newcomers an immediate contact while producing the information needed to organize tables.\nGuests mark their arrival and readiness on a welcome sheet before looking at the available games. The host can distinguish people seeking a table immediately from those who want a little time to settle in.\nA rotating welcome volunteer records arriving guests and their readiness, then gives the host short updates between game starts. The host receives grouped information while arrivals still have someone available to explain the evening."
    }
  ],
